@startuml P330_mdoc_proximity_present
'- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
' Settings
'- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
'=== Header and Footer ===
header OPEN-DID Technical Specification
footer
  	Page %page% of %lastpage% at %date("yyyy-MM-dd hh:mm:ss")
end footer

'=== Title ===
title
	<size:25>P330 : mdoc Proximity Presentation </size>
end title

'=== Options ===
' Auto-numbering: ex) "<b>000." => pads with zeros to display a 3-digit number
autonumber "<b>(#)</b>"
' Hide the participant box at the bottom of the page
'hide footbox

'=== Participants ===
<style>
participant {
  Padding 20
}
</style>
skinparam BoxPadding 20
skinparam MaxMessageSize 500
skinparam MinClassWidth 80

actor "**User**" as USER

box Mobile (Holder) #OldLace
    participant "**CApp**" as CA <<App>> #WhiteSmoke
    participant "**Wallet**" as WALLET <<Wallet>> #WhiteSmoke
    participant "**Proximity SDK**\n(Holder)" as PH <<SDK>> #WhiteSmoke
end box

box mdoc Reader #AliceBlue
    participant "**Proximity SDK**\n(Reader)" as PR <<SDK>> #WhiteSmoke
    participant "**mdoc Reader App**" as RD <<App>> #WhiteSmoke
end box

participant "**Trust Agent**" as TA <<WAS>> #WhiteSmoke

box Trust Repository
    participant "**DID Document**" as BC <<Storage>> #WhiteSmoke
end box

'- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
' Content
'- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
|||

== Preliminary : Trusted Issuer List ==

RD -> TA ++ : Request trusted issuer list
return Trusted issuer list
rnote right of RD #MintCream
    Entry : issuer DID, name, allowed docTypes
end note
RD <-> BC : Retrieve / respond issuer DID Documents
RD -> RD : Store list and DID Documents\
            \n* Replaced only when all are received

== P330-1 : Device Engagement ==

USER -> CA : Start proximity presentation
activate CA
CA -> PH ++ : Start Device Engagement
alt QR
    PH -> RD : Display / scan Device Engagement QR code
else NFC handover
    PH -> PR : Deliver Device Engagement\n(static or negotiated handover)
end
rnote right of PH #Lavender
    For support by OS, refer to 5.1 of [mdoc Proximity Presentation]
end note

== P330-2 : Session Establishment ==

PH <-> PR : Connect transport channel\n(BLE / L2CAP / NFC / Wi-Fi Aware)
PH -> PH : Derive session keys (ECDH + HKDF)
PR -> PR : Derive session keys (ECDH + HKDF)

== P330-3 : DeviceRequest and Matching ==

RD -> PR : Request to send DeviceRequest\n{docType, data elements, intent_to_retain = false}
PR -> PH : DeviceRequest (session encryption)
PH -> CA : DeviceRequest (decrypted)
CA -> WALLET ++ : Request DeviceRequest matching
return Matching result

== P330-4 : DeviceResponse ==

CA -> WALLET ++ : Request DeviceResponse generation
WALLET -> WALLET : Generate DeviceResponse\
            \n* DeviceAuth = deviceSignature (device key signature)
return DeviceResponse
CA -> PH : Request to send DeviceResponse
PH -> PR : DeviceResponse (session encryption)
deactivate PH
deactivate CA

== P330-5 : Verification ==

PR -> RD : Receive DeviceResponse (decrypted)
RD -> PR ++ : Request trust decision and verification for each document\n(using the stored trusted issuer list and issuer DID Documents)
rnote right of PR #MintCream
    Verification order for each document
    1. Check that the kid in the issuerAuth signature header is a DID URL
    2. Check that the DID of the kid is in the trusted issuer list
    3. Check that the docType is in the allowed docTypes
    4. Obtain the public key from the stored issuer DID Document
    5. Verify the issuerAuth signature
    6. Verify DeviceAuth (deviceSignature or deviceMac)
end note
return Verification result
RD -> RD : Display result\
            \n* Issuer trusted or not, DeviceAuth result\
            \n* Validity period, presented data elements

@enduml
